    "status": "present",
    "value": "Maintain mutable array values, take numbered snapshots, and read values from earlier snapshots without copying the entire array per snapshot. The approach is: per-index versioned values, overwrite within current snapshot, predecessor binary search. Its target cost is set/snap amortized O(1), get O(log history), O(length+sets) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
